// parallelism: 1
// Regression test for a `parallel 2` block that ran serialized. The nominal
// degree of a node has a floor of two, so a surrounding scope at actual degree
// one and a `parallel 2` block both read as nominal two. Matching on the
// nominal degree alone fused the scatter into the block and the gather out of
// it, and a fused channel blocks the sender until the receiver's next receive,
// so the two legs lockstep-alternated instead of running concurrently. Both
// boundaries must be tiny (`╎`), not fused (`║`).
from {x: 1}
repeat
optimize_barrier
where true
parallel 2 { where x > 0 }
discard
